# The oldest Supavise release a joined server may run alongside the release being built.
# deploy/release-assets.sh writes it into the signed release manifest as min_peer_from. The rule that
# decides who may join a cluster is cluster.CheckVersionWindow (internal/cluster/version.go), not this
# file: two servers of one cluster have the same major version, differ by at most one minor version
# and pin the same Postgres major version. A join and a rejoin enforce it (the leader answers 409
# version_skew); the ping between servers only raises the node_version_skew alert. The manifest reader
# checks this value and does not enforce it on peers, so it stays v0.0.0 while the window is the rule:
# the release tool refuses a manifest whose min_peer_from is newer than its own version, and the upgrade,
# install, converge and two-server tests sign releases numbered v0.0.x. Servers of one cluster also
# replicate to each other, so a release that changes what they say to each other (a peer API call
# without a fallback, a registry change an older binary cannot read) raises it, in the commit that
# makes the change, together with those tests' version numbers. v0.4.0 adds no peer action or field.
# v0.1.0, v0.1.1 and v0.1.3 are released and have no mesh, so none of them is ever a peer.
v0.0.0
